// 'Veach, Bidir Room' — Benedikt Bitterli (CC0, public domain; crediting
// the artist encouraged). The bidirectional-transport room: both bulbs
// hide inside their fixtures — a torchiere floor lamp throwing the room's
// light off the ceiling, a shaded tube spot on the wall — so almost all
// light arrives indirectly, past a glass egg for good measure. pbrt's own
// oracle integrator for it is bdpt; cenote renders it with a
// unidirectional path tracer, which converges to the same image but earns
// its noise here by design.
// Official pbrt-v4 export from https://benedikt-bitterli.me/resources/ —
// `scenes/corpus/fetch.sh veach-bidir` materializes the source; this RON
// was bootstrapped once by `cenote-cli import
// sources/bitterli/veach-bidir/scene-v4.pbrt` and is the source of truth
// — re-imports diff into scratch, never over it.
//
// Import fidelity: exact in effect — one equal-axis roughness pair
// averaged to itself.
